ents of the Hundred Acre Wood embark on a quest to save Christopher Robin from an imaginary culprit while Pooh deals with a hunger for honey. The film is directed by Stephen Anderson and Don Hall, adapted from Milne\'s books by a story team led by Burny Mattinson, produced by Peter Del Vecho, Clark Spencer, John Lasseter, and Craig Sost, and narrated by John Cleese.', 'score': 0.83837890625, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '19329783', 'title': 'Winnie-the-Pooh', 'contents': 'Winnie-the-Pooh, also called Pooh Bear, is a fictional anthropomorphic teddy bear created by English author A. A. Milne.', 'score': 0.8232421875, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '805401', 'title': 'Sterling Holloway', 'contents': 'Sterling Price Holloway Jr. (January 4, 1905 – November 22, 1992) was an American actor and voice actor who appeared in over 100 films and 40 television shows. He was also a voice actor for The Walt Disney Company, well known for his distinctive tenor voice, and served as the original voice of the title character in Walt Disney\'s "Winnie the Pooh".', 'score': 0.82177734375, 'is_poisoned': False}]
