Elko Regional Airport (IATA: EKO, ICAO: KEKO, FAA LID: EKO) , formerly Elko Municipal Airport, is a mile west of downtown Elko, in Elko County, Nevada.
Elko/Lionel P. Demers Memorial Airpark
Elko/Lionel P. Demers Memorial Airpark, (TC LID: CBE2) , is located 1.7 NM west southwest of Elko, British Columbia, Canada.
El Reno Regional Airport
El Reno Regional Airport (ICAO: KRQO, FAA LID: RQO) is in Canadian County, Oklahoma, five miles southwest of El Reno, which owns it. The FAA's National Plan of Integrated Airport Systems for 2009–2013 categorized it as a "general aviation" facility.
Elk City Regional Business Airport
Elk City Regional Business Airport (IATA: ELK, ICAO: KELK, FAA LID: ELK) is a city-owned public-use airport located one mile northeast of the central business district of Elk CIty, a city in Beckham County, Oklahoma, United States.
Elko, British Columbia
Elko is located at the junction of Highway 93 and the Crowsnest Highway (provincial highway No. 3), to the north of the Roosville Canadian-USA border crossing. A small sawmill town, Elko is situated near the southern end of the Rocky Mountain Trench at the edge of a plateau at the base of the Canadian Rockies, in the East Kootenay region of southeastern British Columbia.

