Zurracapote (sometimes abbreviated as zurra) is a popular Spanish alcoholic mixed drink, similar to sangría. It consists of red wine mixed with fruit such as peaches and lemons, sugar, and cinnamon. The concoction is then traditionally left to steep for several days, though some recipes call for the addition of other alcoholic beverages, juices, and fruit extracts. The result is a mild-to-medium alcoholic drink, similar to sangría.
Barracuda (cocktail)
The Barracuda is an alcoholic cocktail based on Gold rum, Galliano liqueur, pineapple juice, fresh lime juice and top with Prosecco, per IBA specified ingredients.
Tuxedo (cocktail)
The Tuxedo is an IBA Official Cocktail composed of gin, dry Vermouth, orange bitters, maraschino and Absinthe.
El Presidente (cocktail)
The El Presidente is a mix of rum, curaçao, vermouth, and grenadine.
Zucca (aperitif)
Zucca (] ) is a commercial Italian aperitif. Although its name is Zucca, the Italian word for squash, and is featured at Zucca's Bar located in the Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II in Milan, its base ingredient is Rhubarb, hence its name Rabarbaro Zucca. It is also combined with zest, cardamom seeds and other curative herbs. The liqueur has a delicate and pleasant bittersweet taste and is often mixed with soda water and ice.

