Observation 2: Chris Van Hollen
Christopher Van Hollen Jr. (born January 10, 1959) is the junior United States Senator from Maryland, serving since January 3, 2017. From 2003 to 2017, he served as the U.S. Representative for Maryland 's 8 congressional district . He is a member of the Democratic Party.
John C. Van Hollen
John C. Van Hollen (June 27, 1933) is a Wisconsin businessman and politician.
J. B. Van Hollen
John Byron "J. B." Van Hollen (born February 19, 1966) is an American attorney and politician who served as Wisconsin Attorney General from 2007 until 2015. A Republican, he was elected to the office in November 2006 and took office on January 3, 2007, succeeding Democrat Peg Lautenschlager. Van Hollen did not seek reelection in 2014 and left office on January 5, 2015.
Christopher Van Hollen (diplomat)
Christopher Van Hollen Sr. (September 23, 1922 – January 30, 2013) was an American member of the United States Foreign Service who served as the United States Ambassador to Sri Lanka and the Maldives from 1972 until 1976. He was the father of U.S. Senator Chris Van Hollen of Maryland.
DISCLOSE Act
The Democracy Is Strengthened by Casting Light On Spending in Elections Act, commonly known as the DISCLOSE Act and also known as H.R. 5175 (S.3628-Senate), was a bill introduced in the U.S. House of Representatives by Chris Van Hollen (D-Maryland) on April 29, 2010 and in the U.S. Senate by Charles Schumer (D-New York) on July 21, 2010.

