The Importance of Being Icelandic is a 1998 documentary film by the filmmaker Jon Gustafsson (born in Iceland and living in Canada) that traces the steps of three Icelandic Canadians on a different quest of discovering their Icelandic heritage by going to Iceland. In addition to their time in Iceland, he returns with them to Canada and captures their reactions of the Islendingadagurinn celebrated each year at Gimli. The contrasts in perspective between his viewpoint on Canadian culture and that of three Icelandic-Canadians on a quest for their ancestral heritage is at the centre of the documentary.
The Icelandic Dream
The Icelandic Dream (Icelandic: Íslenski draumurinn (   )) is a 2000 Icelandic film directed by Robert Ingi Douglas. The movie depicts the story about an average Icelander and his dream to maintain wealth and fame.
The Honour of the House
The Honour of the House (Icelandic: "Ungfrúin góða og húsið" ) is a 1999 Icelandic film directed by Guðný Halldórsdóttir. It was Iceland's official Best Foreign Language Film submission at the 72nd Academy Awards, but did not manage to receive a nomination.
List of Icelandic films of 2014
The Icelandic film industry produced over twenty feature films in 2014. This article fully lists all non-pornographic films, including short films, that had a release date in that year and which were at least partly made by Iceland. It does not include films first released in previous years that had release dates in 2014. <br> Also included is an overview of the major events in Icelandic film, including film festivals and awards ceremonies, as well as lists of those films that have been particularly well received, both critically and financially.
Thicker than Water (2006 film)
Thicker than Water (original title: Blóðbönd (   )) is a 2006 Icelandic film.

[Retriever Results] [{'id': '3943529', 'title': 'The Five Obstructions', 'contents': 'The Five Obstructions is a 2003 Danish documentary film directed by Lars von Trier and Jørgen Leth. The film is conceived as a documentary, but incorporates lengthy sections of experimental films produced by the filmmakers. The premise is that von Trier has created a challenge for his friend and mentor, Jørgen Leth, another renowned filmmaker. von Trier\'s favorite film is Leth\'s "The Perfect Human" (1967), and von Trier gives Leth the task of remaking "The Perfect Human" five times, each time with a different "obstruction" (or obstacle) imposed by von Trier.', 'score': 0.85400390625, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '9310096', 'title': 'Five (2003 film)', 'contents': 'Five (Persian: پنج\u200e \u200e "Panj"), also known as Five Dedicated to Ozu, is a 2003 Iranian documentary film directed by Abbas Kiarostami. The film consists of five long shots, averaging about 16 minutes each. Four of the five have fixed camera positions.', 'score': 0.81591796875, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '1138292', 'title': '5x2', 'contents': '5x2 (also "Cinq fois deux"; English: Five Times Two ) is a 2004 French film directed by François Ozon, which uncovers the back story to the gradual disintegration of a middle class marriage by depicting five key moments in the relationship, but in reverse order.', 'score': 0.81005859375, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '45027726', 'title': 'Fifth Column Films', 'contents': 'Fifth Column Films is a UK film production company best known for feature documentaries Way of the Morris and TEMPEST.', 'score': 0.80712890625, 'is_poisoned': False}, {'id': '35518735', 'title': 'Five Have a Mystery to Solve (film)', 'contents': "Five Have a Mystery to Solve is a 6-part 1964 British film serial made by the Children's Film Foundation, based on the novel of the same name by Enid Blyton.", 'score': 0.80712890625, 'is_poisoned': False}]
